2. In these Rules —
“Council member” means a member of the Council;
“family respondent” means a person against whom a family exclusion order or family visit limit is sought or made;
“review committee” means a committee appointed by the Council under section 155(8) of the Act for the purposes mentioned in rule 11;
“secretary” means the secretary to the Council appointed under section 155(2) of the Act;
“third party respondent” means a person against whom a third party exclusion order or third party visit limit is proposed or made.

3. The secretary must keep and maintain —
(a)the following records relating to family exclusion orders and family visit limits:
(i)records of every application to the Council for a family exclusion order under section 162 of the Act or for a family visit limit under section 163A of the Act;
(ii)records of every application to set aside any family exclusion order or family visit limit under section 165C(3) of the Act;
(iii)records of every application to vary or revoke a family exclusion order or a family visit limit under rule 34;
(b)the following records relating to third party exclusion orders and third party visit limits:
(i)records of information leading to a third party exclusion order or a third party visit limit made by a Committee of Assessors;
(ii)records of every objection under rule 42, or appeal under rule 46, against a third party exclusion order or a third party visit limit;
(iii)records of every application to set aside any third party exclusion order or third party visit limit under section 165C(3) of the Act;
(iv)records of every application to vary or revoke a third party exclusion order or a third party visit limit under rule 48;
(c)the following records relating to self‑exclusions and voluntary visit limits:
(i)records of every application under section 165AA(1) of the Act for a self‑exclusion;
(ii)records of every application under section 165B(1) of the Act for a voluntary visit limit (or a variation of a voluntary visit limit);
(iii)records of every application to the Council to revoke any self‑exclusion under section 165AA(3) of the Act or to revoke a voluntary visit limit under section 165B(3A) of the Act;
(d)all records of proceedings made under rule 19 or 26;
(e)records of the list of excluded persons established and maintained under section 168 of the Act, as varied or updated from time to time;
(f)records of the register of excluded persons and visit limited persons kept and maintained under rule 3 of the Casino Control (Problem Gambling — Exclusion Orders and Visit Limits) Rules 2008 (G.N. No. S 623/2008) as in force before 21 September 2026; and
(g)such other records as the chairperson may direct.

11. The Council may appoint one or more committees under section 155(8) of the Act each as a review committee for the purposes of performing all or any of the following functions or powers of the Council:
(a)to grant permission under section 160(a) or (b)(ii) of the Act;
(b)to grant permission under section 161(a) of the Act;
(c)to decide any appeal under section 165(10) of the Act;
(d)to grant permission under section 166(2) of the Act;
(e)to decide any application for variation or revocation under section 166(1) of the Act;
(f)to revoke any self‑exclusion and impose any condition under section 165AA of the Act;
(g)to revoke any voluntary visit limit and impose any condition under section 165B of the Act.

19.—(1) The record of the proceedings of a review committee is to include —
(a)the name and particulars of every person who participated in the proceedings;
(b)the name and particulars of every person who was requested to participate in the proceedings but failed to do so;
(c)a summary of the evidence presented by or on behalf of each party to the proceedings in sufficient detail to enable the Council to comprehend the course of the proceedings;
(d)the reason for any adjournment;
(e)any other information relevant to the decision of the review committee;
(f)the decision reached by the review committee and the reasons for its decision; and
(g)the terms of any family exclusion order, family visit limit, third party exclusion order or third party visit limit made or varied.
(2) The record of proceedings is to be signed by the chairperson of the review committee and all the other members of the committee.
(3) A summary of the record of proceedings (including the decision reached by the review committee and the reasons for its decision) must be submitted to the Council.

26.—(1) The record of the proceedings of a Committee of Assessors is to include —
(a)the name and particulars of every person who participated in the proceedings;
(b)the name and particulars of every person who was requested to participate in the proceedings but failed to do so;
(c)a summary of the evidence presented by or on behalf of each party to the proceedings in sufficient detail to enable the Council to comprehend the course of the proceedings;
(d)the reason for any adjournment;
(e)any other information relevant to the decision of the Committee;
(f)the decision reached by the Committee and the reasons for its decision; and
(g)the terms of any family exclusion order, provisional family exclusion order, family visit limit, third party exclusion order or third party visit limit made.
(2) The record of proceedings is to be signed by the chairperson of the Committee of Assessors and all the other members of the Committee.
(3) A summary of the record of proceedings (including the decision reached by the Committee of Assessors and the reasons for its decision) must be submitted to the Council.

38. Where a Committee of Assessors decides to conduct an oral hearing for an application referred to the Committee under section 159(2) or 163A(2) of the Act or for an application to set aside a family exclusion order or family visit limit under section 165C(3) of the Act, the Committee is to conduct that hearing in the manner set out below —
(a)the chairperson of the Committee of Assessors is to give a brief statement of the facts of the application;
(b)the Committee of Assessors must have regard to and consider the evidence of —
(i)the person who applied for the family exclusion order or family visit limit (including any person who applied for the family exclusion order or family visit limit on behalf of another person under section 160(b) or 161 of the Act);
(ii)the family respondent; and
(iii)such other person as the Committee of Assessors may think relevant to determine the application;
(c)where any person was requested to attend the proceedings but fails to do so, or states that he or she does not wish to be present at the proceedings, the chairperson of the Committee of Assessors must make a note of that fact in the record of proceedings; and
(d)the person who applied for the family exclusion order or family visit limit (including any person who applied for the family exclusion order or family visit limit on behalf of another person under section 160(b) or 161 of the Act) and the family respondent may, with the permission of the chairperson of the Committee of Assessors, produce one or more witnesses to give evidence on matters relating to the application.

39. Where the Council has delegated to a review committee the power to determine an application to vary or revoke a family exclusion order or family visit limit under section 166(1)(a) of the Act and the review committee decides to conduct an oral hearing for the application, the review committee is to conduct that hearing in the manner set out below —
(a)the chairperson of the review committee is to give a brief statement of the facts of the application;
(b)the review committee must have regard to and consider the evidence of —
(i)the person who applied for the family exclusion order or family visit limit (including any person who applied for the family exclusion order or family visit limit on behalf of another person under section 160(b) or 161 of the Act);
(ii)the family respondent; and
(iii)such other person as the review committee may think relevant to determine the application;
(c)where any person was requested to attend the proceedings but fails to do so, or states that the person does not wish to be present at the proceedings, the chairperson of the review committee must make a note of that fact in the record of proceedings; and
(d)the person who applied for the family exclusion order or family visit limit (including any person who applied for the family exclusion order or family visit limit on behalf of another person under section 160(b) or 161 of the Act) and the family respondent may, with the permission of the chairperson of the review committee, produce one or more witnesses to give evidence on matters relating to the application.
